# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Visual Automata Studio — Environment Variables
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# This project uses a fully local authentication system backed by the browser's
# localStorage and the Web Crypto API (SubtleCrypto / PBKDF2).
#
# No external service, no backend, and no environment variables are required
# to run the application. Authentication works entirely offline out of the box.
#
# ── What is stored ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
#   vas_users_v1      User accounts (email, display name, PBKDF2 password hash)
#   vas_session_v1    Active session (user ID + expiry, 30-day TTL)
#   vas_progress_<id> Per-user learning progress (namespaced by user ID)
#   vas-theme         UI colour scheme preference
#
# ── Security notes ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
#   Passwords are hashed with PBKDF2 + SHA-256 (200 000 iterations, random salt)
#   using the browser's native SubtleCrypto API. Plain-text passwords are never
#   stored anywhere.
#
#   Data is scoped to the browser/profile. Clearing localStorage removes all
#   accounts and progress — warn users before they use "Clear site data".
#
# ── Optional: future cloud integration ───────────────────────────────────────
#
# If you later want to sync progress across devices, you can swap in a cloud
# StorageAdapter (e.g. Supabase, Firebase) without touching any auth logic —
# the StorageAdapter interface in src/features/learning/storageAdapter.ts is
# designed for exactly this.
#
# Example variables for a future Supabase integration:
#   VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project.supabase.co
#   VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-anon-key-here
#
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
